we help you speak clear, natural English with confidence in real life and professional situations.

6
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:41,360
If you enjoy this lesson, please give us a thumbs up, and don't forget to subscribe.

7
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:45,520
Yes, your support really helps us create more lessons like this.

8
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,840
Thank you so much for being here.

9
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:50,160
So, Jack, what are we talking about today?

10
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,240
Today we have a very practical and important topic.

11
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:58,240
We're going to learn how to talk about your job in business English.

12
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:02,640
I love this topic because it's something everyone needs,

13
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:09,280
Whether you're networking in a meeting or at a job interview, you always need to talk about your job.

14
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:15,600
Exactly. And sometimes people know English, but they don't know how to explain what they do clearly.

15
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:22,800
Yes, they might say something very short, like, I work in IT, but they don't explain anything more.

16
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:26,080
Or they feel nervous and forget simple words.

17
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:30,720
Don't worry. Today we'll show you how to talk about your job step by step

18
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:33,120
in a natural and professional way.

19
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:39,280
And we'll use a lot of real examples so you can actually use these phrases in your daily life.

20
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,440
Sounds great!

21
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:44,280
So, Jack, let's start with the most common situation.

22
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:47,280
You meet someone new. What do they ask you?

23
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:50,080
The most common question is, what do you do?

24
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:53,560
Yes, it's simple, short and very natural.

25
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:59,120
Some learners say, what is your job, which is correct, but it sounds more formal.

26
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:03,920
Right. In everyday conversation, what do you do is the best choice.

27
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:06,720
Okay, so how do we answer this question?

28
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:11,320
The simplest way is to say, I'm a plus your job title.

29
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:14,320
For example, I'm a software engineer.

30
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:16,720
Or I'm a sales manager.

31
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,620
Or I'm an accountant.

32
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:23,720
Very good. And remember to use a or an. That's important.

33
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:27,620
Yes, don't forget that small word. It makes a big difference.

34
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:29,660
Now let's make it more interesting.

35
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:32,960
Don't just say your job title. Add more information.

36
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:36,660
Exactly. You can say what you do in your job.

37
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:39,360
For example, I'm a project manager.

38
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:42,360
I manage teams and coordinate projects.

39
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:45,260
Or I'm a customer service representative.

40
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:47,560
I help customers solve problems.

41
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,060
That sounds much better.

42
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:51,360
It gives a clear picture of your work.

43
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:52,920
Let's do a quick practice.

44
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:54,360
Emily, what do you do?

45
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:55,860
I'm an English teacher.

46
00:02:55,860 --> 00:02:59,860
I help professionals improve their communication skills.

47
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:02,860
That's a great answer! Clear and professional.

48
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:04,860
Your turn. What do you do?

49
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:09,860
I'm a content creator. I create educational videos and write scripts.

50
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:12,860
Perfect! See how easy that is?

51
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:16,860
Now let's talk about where you work, because that's another common question.

52
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:19,860
Yes. People often ask, where do you work?

53
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:21,860
You can answer in a few ways.

54
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:24,860
You can say, I work at, plus a place.

55
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:25,860
place.

56
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:29,220
For example, I work at a marketing agency.

57
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:31,620
Or I work at a hospital.

58
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:35,220
You can also say I work for plus a company.

59
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:38,700
Like I work for a multinational company.

60
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:41,020
Or I work for a startup.

61
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:43,980
And don't forget, you can say I work from home.

62
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:46,700
Yes, that's very common these days.

63
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:48,500
Let's give a full example.

64
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:53,860
I'm a software developer, I work for a tech company, and I mostly work from home.

65
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:56,300
That's a strong, complete answer.

66
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:57,700
Now let's go deeper.

67
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:00,620
How do you describe your daily tasks?

68
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:04,160
This is where you can really improve your business English.

69
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:07,900
You can say, my main responsibility is to...

70
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:13,040
For example, my main responsibility is to manage client accounts.

71
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:18,420
Or my responsibilities include preparing reports and analyzing data.

72
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:20,220
Let's give more examples.

73
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:23,740
I organize meetings and communicate with clients.

74
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:27,700
I design marketing campaigns and track performance.

75
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:31,260
I develop software and fix technical issues.

76
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:37,140
Notice how we use simple verbs like manage, organize, design, develop.

77
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:39,740
Yes, simple verbs are powerful.

78
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:41,460
Now let's talk about your team.

79
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:43,900
Do you work alone or with others?

80
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:45,020
Good point.

81
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:48,620
You can say, I work with a team of five.

82
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:51,860
Or I collaborate with different departments.

83
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:54,380
Or I work independently.

84
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:57,800
And if you're the leader, you can say, I manage a team.

85
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:01,860
For example, I manage a team of sales representatives.

86
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:03,980
That sounds very professional.

87
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:06,380
Now let's talk about your work schedule.

88
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:10,040
Yes, this is also very common in conversation.

89
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,620
You can say, I work full-time.

90
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:14,700
Or I work part-time.

91
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:16,900
You can also describe your hours.

92
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:19,300
I work from nine to five.

93
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:22,240
I start at 8 and finish at 4.

94
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:27,720
And if your schedule is flexible, you can say, I have flexible working hours.

95
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:29,440
That's a great benefit.

96
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:31,840
Now let's talk about something more personal.

97
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:34,040
What do you like about your job?

98
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:38,080
This is important, especially in interviews or networking.

99
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:40,380
You can say, I enjoy.

100
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:43,640
For example, I enjoy working with people.

101
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:46,380
Or I enjoy solving problems.

102
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:50,100
Or I enjoy the creative aspect of my job.

103
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:52,220
You can also say, I like.

104
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:54,020
I like my team.

105
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,100
I like the work environment.

106
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:58,860
I like the opportunities to learn.

107
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,860
Now what about challenges?

108
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:03,820
Yes, every job has challenges.

109
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:06,620
You can say, one challenge is...

110
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:11,300
For example, one challenge is managing tight deadlines.

111
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:14,500
Or it can be stressful during busy periods.

112
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:18,580
Or sometimes I have to deal with difficult clients.

113
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:21,300
Notice how we stay professional and polite.

114
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:24,700
Yes, we don't say I hate my job.

115
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:25,700
Exactly.

116
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:27,380
That sounds too negative.

117
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:29,820
Now let's do a real-life example.

118
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:30,820
Okay.

119
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:33,060
Imagine you're at a business event.

120
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,060
I'll start.

121
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,580
Hi, I'm Jack.

122
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:36,580
Nice to meet you.

123
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:37,580
Hi, Jack.

124
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:38,580
I'm Emily.

125
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:40,080
Nice to meet you, too.

126
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:41,500
So what do you do?

127
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,740
I'm a human resources deshlist.

128
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:46,500
I work for an international company.

129
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:47,900
That sounds interesting.

130
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:49,380
What do you do in your role?

131
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:52,580
I handle recruitment and employee relations.

132
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:55,580
I also organize training programs.

133
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:56,580
That's great.

134
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:57,860
Do you enjoy your job?

135
00:06:57,860 --> 00:07:03,260
Yes, I really enjoy working with people and helping them grow in their careers.

136
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:04,820
That's a perfect answer.

137
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:08,380
Yes, and it sounds natural and confident.

138
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:11,620
Now let's try a slightly more advanced example.

139
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:12,620
Okay.

140
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:13,980
Hi, what do you do?

141
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:15,900
I'm a financial analyst.

142
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:18,700
I work for a large investment firm.

143
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,900
What are your main responsibilities?

144
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:26,540
I analyze financial data, prepare reports, and support decision-making.

145
00:07:26,540 --> 00:07:28,040
That sounds challenging.

146
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:33,820
Yes, it can be, especially when working under tight deadlines, but I enjoy the analytical

147
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:34,820
aspect.

148
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:36,780
That's very professional.

149
00:07:36,780 --> 00:07:38,940
Now let's talk about career goals.

150
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:42,460
Yes, this is very common in interviews.

151
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:49,340
You can say, I'd like to, for example, I'd like to grow in my role, or I'd like to take

152
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:55,060
on more responsibility, or I'd like to become a manager in the future.

153
00:07:55,060 --> 00:08:01,260
You can also say, I'm working towards, I'm working towards a promotion, or I'm working

154
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:03,840
towards improving my skills.

155
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,540
That shows ambition.

156
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:09,640
Now let's do one final full conversation example.

157
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:10,640
Great idea.

158
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:12,520
Hi, nice to meet you.

159
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:14,000
Nice to meet you too.

160
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,180
What do you do?

161
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:16,920
I'm a marketing specialist.

162
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:19,320
I work for a digital agency.

163
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:21,260
What does your job involve?

164
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:25,400
I create marketing campaigns, manage social media accounts,

165
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,780
and analyze performance data.

166
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:29,120
That sounds interesting.

167
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,440
Do you enjoy it?

168
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,680
Yes, I enjoy the creative work

169
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:35,040
and working with different clients.

170
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:37,120
What's the most challenging part?

171
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:39,480
Managing deadlines can be stressful,

172
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:42,640
especially when working on multiple projects.

173
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:43,860
I understand.

174
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:45,560
What are your future goals?

175
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:47,760
I like to become a marketing manager

176
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:49,640
and lead my own team.

177
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:51,560
That's an excellent answer.

178
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:55,440
Yes, and it uses simple, clear business English.

179
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:57,560
That's the key message today.

180
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:58,900
Keep it simple.

181
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:00,160
Be clear.

182
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:01,880
And be confident.

183
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:05,160
You don't need perfect English to talk about your job.

184
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:08,400
You just need the right phrases and practice.

185
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:11,560
And the more you practice, the easier it becomes.

186
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:14,840
So next time someone asks, what do you do?

187
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:16,240
You'll be ready.

188
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,800
That's all for today.

189
