215
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:39,800
With real examples, real phrases, and realistic situations.

216
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:40,800
Exactly.

217
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:43,960
So Daniel, let me ask you something to start.

218
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:44,960
Go ahead.

219
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:50,640
When someone asks you about your job, do you give a short answer or a detailed one?

220
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:52,480
It depends on the situation.

221
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:58,000
If it's casual, I keep it short, but in business settings, I give more details.

222
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,560
That's a great point.

223
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:05,120
matters. Exactly. So let's start from the most basic question. The classic one.

224
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:12,580
Yes, the question everyone hears. What do you do? Simple, short, and very common. So

225
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:17,220
Emma, what do you do? I'm a business English trainer. I work with

226
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:21,740
professionals to help them communicate more effectively in English. That's a

227
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:27,380
great answer. Notice it's not just the job title. You added value. Exactly.

228
00:11:27,380 --> 00:11:34,240
Just saying, I'm a teacher is okay, but adding more detail makes your answer stronger.

229
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:35,340
Let me try.

230
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:36,340
What do you do?

231
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:37,340
Go ahead.

232
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,860
I'm a project manager.

233
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:43,940
I manage cross-functional teams and ensure projects are delivered on time.

234
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:45,980
That sounds very professional.

235
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:46,980
Thank you.

236
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:50,040
So everyone listening, here's your first tip.

237
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,220
Don't stop at your job title.

238
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:54,620
Add one sentence about what you do.

239
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:58,060
Yes, it makes you sound more confident and clear.

240
00:11:58,060 --> 00:12:01,100
Now let's talk about another common question.

241
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:02,460
Where do you work?

242
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:03,500
Exactly.

243
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,380
Daniel, where do you work?

244
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:08,420
I work for a multinational technology company.

245
00:12:08,420 --> 00:12:11,340
We develop software solutions for businesses.

246
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:12,260
Nice.

247
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:15,820
You used work for, which is correct for companies.

248
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:16,420
Right.

249
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:18,620
And you can also say, I work at,

250
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:20,500
if you mention the company name.

251
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:24,860
For example, I work at a training institute in Singapore.

252
00:12:24,860 --> 00:12:29,260
Or I work at a startup that focuses on FinTech solutions.

253
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:30,260
Perfect.

254
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:31,660
Now let's go deeper.

255
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:33,820
Yes, let's make it more real.

256
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:36,260
Imagine you're at a networking event.

257
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:38,100
Someone asks you about your job.

258
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:39,740
Okay, I'll start.

259
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:40,740
Go ahead.

260
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:41,740
Hi.

261
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:42,740
Nice to meet you too.

262
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:43,740
What do you do?

263
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:44,740
Hi.

264
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:45,740
Nice to meet you too.

265
00:12:45,740 --> 00:12:47,340
I'm a financial analyst.

266
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:52,620
I work for an investment firm and I analyze market trends to help clients make better

267
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:54,500
investment decisions.

268
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:57,540
That's a strong answer, clear and professional.

269
00:12:57,540 --> 00:12:58,540
Thank you.

270
00:12:58,540 --> 00:12:59,540
Now your turn.

271
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:01,620
I'm a Human Resources Manager.

272
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:06,740
I handle recruitment, employee relations, and staff development programs.

273
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:07,740
Excellent.

274
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:10,060
Notice how specific that is.

275
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:13,100
Yes, specificity makes a big difference.

276
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:16,660
Now let's talk about describing your daily tasks.

277
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:18,980
This is where many learners struggle.

278
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:19,980
Exactly.

279
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:23,420
They don't know how to explain what they actually do.

280
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:26,680
So Emma, what are your daily responsibilities?

281
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:32,580
My main responsibilities include conducting training sessions, preparing lesson materials

282
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:35,180
and coaching clients one-on-one.

283
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:36,180
That's great.

284
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:39,100
You used my main responsibilities include.

285
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:41,780
Yes, that's a very useful phrase.

286
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:43,580
Let me give another example.

287
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:44,580
Go ahead.

288
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:49,700
This role involves coordinating with different departments, managing timelines, and ensuring

289
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:51,900
project goals are met.

290
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:53,140
Very professional.

291
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:54,140
Thank you.

292
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:56,460
Now let's make it more practical.

293
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:59,460
Imagine you're explaining your job to a new colleague.

294
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:00,460
Okay.

295
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:01,460
I'll start.

296
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:02,460
Sure.

297
00:14:02,460 --> 00:14:03,980
Hi, I just joined the company.

298
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,500
Can you tell me what you do?

299
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:06,500
Of course.

300
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,020
I'm in the marketing department.

301
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:13,700
I focus on digital campaigns, social media strategy, and content creation.

302
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:20,420
clear and helpful. Thanks. What about you? I work in operations. I manage workflows,

303
00:14:20,420 --> 00:14:26,980
improve processes, and make sure everything runs smoothly. Nice. That sounds very efficient.

304
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:33,380
Now let's talk about talking about your team. Yes, this is very common in business conversations.

305
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:38,820
Daniel, do you work alone or with a team? I work with a team of about 10 people.

306
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:41,140
We collaborate on different projects.

307
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:45,220
Good. You used collaborate, which is a great business word.

308
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:46,340
What about you?

309
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:52,500
I mostly work with clients, but I also collaborate with other trainers and content creators.

310
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:56,500
That's interesting. Now let's talk about describing your company.

311
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,260
Another important skill.

312
00:14:58,260 --> 00:15:00,900
Daniel, how would you describe your company?

313
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:06,340
It's a fast-growing tech company that specializes in AI-driven solutions.

314
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:07,700
That sounds impressive.

315
00:15:07,700 --> 00:15:14,660
Thank you. Let me try. My company is a professional training organization that focuses on corporate

316
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:21,060
communication and leadership skills. Very clear and professional. Now let's move into a slightly

317
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:27,540
more advanced conversation. Okay, let's make it more real. Imagine you're talking to a client.

318
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:32,820
Good scenario. I'll start. Go ahead. Could you tell me a bit about your role?

319
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:39,380
Sure. I'm the head of operations. I oversee daily business activities and ensure efficiency

320
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:41,380
across all departments.

321
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:43,060
That's a strong answer.

322
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:45,020
Thank you. And what about you?

323
00:15:45,020 --> 00:15:50,520
I'm responsible for client relations. I work closely with clients to understand their

324
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:53,860
needs and deliver customized solutions.

325
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:55,940
That sounds very client-focused.

326
00:15:55,940 --> 00:15:56,940
Exactly.

327
00:15:56,940 --> 00:15:59,140
Now let's talk about experience.

328
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:02,580
Yes, this is very important in business English.

329
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:05,160
Emma, how much experience do you have?

330
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:10,620
I have over eight years of experience in corporate training and language education.

331
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:12,020
That sounds impressive.

332
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:13,020
Thank you.

333
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:14,020
What about you?

334
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:18,820
I have about ten years of experience in project management and team leadership.

335
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:19,820
Great!

336
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:22,580
Notice how we say years of experience.

337
00:16:22,580 --> 00:16:25,260
Yes, not years experience.

338
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:27,940
Now let's talk about career progression.

339
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:30,740
This is useful in interviews and networking.

340
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:33,340
Daniel, how did you get into your field?

341
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:39,140
I started as a junior analyst, then moved into project coordination and eventually became

342
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:40,980
a project manager.

343
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:42,740
That's a great career path.

344
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:43,740
Thank you.

345
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:44,740
What about you?

346
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:50,780
I began as an English teacher, then specialized in business communication, and now I work

347
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:52,940
with corporate clients globally.

348
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:54,260
That shows growth.

349
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:55,260
Exactly.

350
00:16:55,260 --> 00:16:57,340
Now let's talk about challenges.

351
00:16:57,340 --> 00:17:00,980
Yes, real conversations include challenges.

352
00:17:00,980 --> 00:17:03,700
What's the most challenging part of your job?

353
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:06,180
Managing different client expectations

354
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:09,580
can be challenging, especially when timelines are tight.

355
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:11,020
That's very real.

356
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:12,180
What about you?

357
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:15,020
Balancing multiple projects at the same time

358
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:18,660
can be stressful, but it also helps me stay organized.

359
00:17:18,660 --> 00:17:19,340
Good.

360
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:21,820
You turned a challenge into a positive.

361
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:24,340
That's important in business communication.

362
00:17:24,340 --> 00:17:26,780
Now let's talk about what you enjoy.

363
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:29,900
Yes, this makes conversations more human.

364
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:32,340
What do you enjoy most about your job?

365
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:35,940
I enjoy solving problems and working with different teams.

366
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:37,420
Every day is different.

367
00:17:37,420 --> 00:17:38,300
Nice.

368
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:39,420
What about you?

369
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:42,860
I enjoy helping people improve their communication skills.

370
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:44,380
It's very rewarding.

371
00:17:44,380 --> 00:17:45,580
That's meaningful.

372
00:17:45,580 --> 00:17:49,260
Now let's do a longer, more natural conversation.

373
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:50,380
Great idea.

374
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:51,260
I'll start.

375
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:52,100
Go ahead.

376
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:53,860
Hi, it's great to meet you.

377
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:55,220
Nice to meet you too.

378
00:17:55,220 --> 00:17:56,760
So what do you do?

379
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:59,080
I'm a business development manager.

380
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:00,840
I work for a consulting firm,

381
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:03,960
and my role is to identify new opportunities

382
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:06,320
and build relationships with clients.

383
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:07,640
That sounds interesting.

384
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:09,320
How long have you been doing that?

385
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:11,060
About five years now.

386
00:18:11,060 --> 00:18:12,520
I started in sales

387
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:15,680
and gradually moved into business development.

388
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:16,680
What about you?

389
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:18,800
I'm a communication specialist.

390
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:20,960
I focus on internal communication

391
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:22,680
and employee engagement.

392
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,880
That's important for company culture.

393
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:25,940
Yes, it is.

394
00:18:25,940 --> 00:18:29,260
I work closely with HR and leadership teams.

395
00:18:29,260 --> 00:18:30,780
Do you enjoy your job?

396
00:18:30,780 --> 00:18:31,780
I do.

397
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:37,020
I especially enjoy working on new initiatives and improving communication strategies.

398
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:38,020
That's great.

399
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:39,740
What's the most challenging?

400
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:43,660
Aligning communication across different departments can be tricky.

401
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,180
I can imagine.

402
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:46,180
What about you?

403
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:48,540
What's challenging in your role?

404
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:53,540
Building long-term client relationships takes time and effort, but it's very rewarding

405
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:55,180
when it works.

406
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:58,180
So where do you see yourself in the future?

407
00:18:58,180 --> 00:19:02,180
I'd like to move into a leadership role and manage a communications team.

408
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:04,180
That sounds like a great goal.

409
00:19:04,180 --> 00:19:06,180
Thank you. What about you?

410
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:11,180
I'd like to expand into international markets and work with global clients.

411
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:13,180
That's exciting. Yes, it is.

412
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:17,180
This is a great example of a natural business conversation.

413
00:19:17,180 --> 00:19:21,180
Yes, and notice how we didn't use complicated language.

414
00:19:21,180 --> 00:19:23,180
Simple, clear, and confident.

415
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,180
and confident.

416
00:19:24,180 --> 00:19:25,300
Exactly.

417
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:27,720
All right, everyone, that's all for today.

418
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:29,620
Thank you so much for listening.

419
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:31,660
Keep practicing, keep improving,

420
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:34,100
and keep speaking English every day.

421
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:36,180
We'll see you in the next episode.

422
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:37,340
Goodbye, everyone.

423
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:43,600
Goodbye.

424
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:44,680
Hello, everyone.

425
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:47,480
We're really happy to have you with us today.

426
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:48,400
Hi, everyone.

427
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,600
Thanks for joining us.

428
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:52,040
If you're here to improve your business English

429
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,760
and learn how to talk about your job

430
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:57,320
clearly and confidently, you're in the right place.

431
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:58,680
I'm Sarah.

432
00:19:58,680 --> 00:20:00,200
And I'm Daniel.

433
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:06,440
On this channel, we help you speak natural, professional English in real-life situations.

434
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:10,640
If you enjoy this lesson, don't forget to give us a thumbs up and subscribe.

435
00:20:10,640 --> 00:20:13,600
Yes, your support helps us a lot.

436
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:15,240
Thank you for being here.

437
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:18,540
So Sarah, what are we talking about today?

438
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:24,040
Today we have a very practical and essential topic, how to talk about your job in business

439
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,480
English.

440
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,660
This is such an important skill.

441
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:32,460
Whether you're in a meeting, a job interview, or a networking event, you need to talk about

442
00:20:32,460 --> 00:20:34,300
your job clearly.

443
00:20:34,300 --> 00:20:35,460
Exactly.

444
00:20:35,460 --> 00:20:38,580
And not just your job title, but what you actually do.

445
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:42,400
Your responsibilities, your experience, and your goals.

446
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:47,300
And the good news is, we're going to make it simple, practical, and easy to follow.

447
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:53,820
Yes, we'll give you useful phrases, real examples, and lots of practice conversations.

448
00:20:53,820 --> 00:20:54,900
Sounds perfect.

449
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:58,540
So Sarah, before we start, how are you feeling today?

450
00:20:58,540 --> 00:20:59,580
I'm feeling great.

451
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:03,980
I'm excited because this topic is something everyone can use immediately.

452
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:04,980
How about you?

453
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:06,540
I'm doing well too.

454
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:11,020
I think our listeners are going to gain a lot of confidence from this episode.

455
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:12,020
I agree.

456
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:14,540
Alright everyone, let's get started.

457
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:17,280
Let's begin with the most common question.

458
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:20,980
How do you ask someone about their job in a business setting?

459
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:26,030
The most natural and common question is, what do you do?

460
00:21:26,030 --> 00:21:27,230
Simple and effective.

461
00:21:27,230 --> 00:21:31,310
Yes, it's short, polite, and widely used.

462
00:21:31,310 --> 00:21:34,150
Can we also say what is your job?

463
00:21:34,150 --> 00:21:39,110
You can, but it sounds more formal and less natural in conversation.

464
00:21:39,110 --> 00:21:41,990
So what do you do is the best choice?

465
00:21:41,990 --> 00:21:42,990
Exactly.

466
00:21:42,990 --> 00:21:46,150
You can also say, what do you do for a living?

467
00:21:46,150 --> 00:21:49,790
That sounds slightly more formal, but still very common.

468
00:21:49,790 --> 00:21:52,590
Okay, now how do we answer that question?

469
00:21:52,590 --> 00:21:54,690
The simplest way is to say,

470
00:21:54,690 --> 00:21:57,490
I'm a plus your job title.

471
00:21:57,490 --> 00:22:00,390
For example, I'm a project manager.

472
00:22:00,390 --> 00:22:02,490
Or I'm an accountant.

473
00:22:02,490 --> 00:22:03,490
Easy.

474
00:22:03,490 --> 00:22:06,890
But in business we often need to say more, right?

475
00:22:06,890 --> 00:22:10,990
Exactly. You should add details to sound more professional.

476
00:22:10,990 --> 00:22:12,690
Can you give an example?

477
00:22:12,690 --> 00:22:15,290
Sure. I'm a project manager.

478
00:22:15,290 --> 00:22:19,190
I manage a team and oversee project timelines.

479
00:22:19,190 --> 00:22:21,190
That sounds much more complete.

480
00:22:21,190 --> 00:22:24,190
Yes, it gives a clearer picture of your role.

481
00:22:24,190 --> 00:22:27,190
Let's give more examples for different jobs.

482
00:22:27,190 --> 00:22:30,190
Okay, I'm a sales executive.

483
00:22:30,190 --> 00:22:33,190
I handle client relationships and close deals.

484
00:22:33,190 --> 00:22:34,190
Nice.

485
00:22:34,190 --> 00:22:36,190
I'm a software developer.

486
00:22:36,190 --> 00:22:39,190
I build and maintain web applications.

487
00:22:39,190 --> 00:22:40,190
Good one.

488
00:22:40,190 --> 00:22:42,190
I'm an HR specialist.

489
00:22:42,190 --> 00:22:45,190
I manage recruitment and employee relations.

490
00:22:45,190 --> 00:22:47,190
These are very practical.

491
00:22:47,190 --> 00:22:50,190
Now let's talk about where you work.

492
00:22:50,190 --> 00:22:54,190
Yes, this is another common question. Where do you work?

493
00:22:54,190 --> 00:22:56,190
How do we answer it?

494
00:22:56,190 --> 00:22:59,190
You can say, I work at for a company.

495
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:03,190
For example, I work at a multinational company.

496
00:23:03,190 --> 00:23:07,190
Or I work for to emphasize the employer.

497
00:23:07,190 --> 00:23:09,190
I work for a tech startup.

498
00:23:09,190 --> 00:23:10,190
Exactly.

499
00:23:10,190 --> 00:23:12,190
What about I work in?

500
00:23:12,190 --> 00:23:16,190
Use in for industries or types of workplaces.

501
00:23:16,190 --> 00:23:20,950
Like, I work in finance, or I work in an office.

502
00:23:20,950 --> 00:23:22,450
Perfect.

503
00:23:22,450 --> 00:23:26,170
Now let's talk about describing your responsibilities.

504
00:23:26,170 --> 00:23:30,070
This is where business English becomes very important.

505
00:23:30,070 --> 00:23:32,550
Because this shows your real value.

506
00:23:32,550 --> 00:23:33,610
Exactly.

507
00:23:33,610 --> 00:23:37,630
You can say, my main responsibility is to…

508
00:23:37,630 --> 00:23:42,490
For example, my main responsibility is to manage client accounts.

509
00:23:42,490 --> 00:23:46,730
Or I'm responsible for preparing financial reports.

510
00:23:46,730 --> 00:23:50,330
Or I handle customer inquiries and support.

511
00:23:50,330 --> 00:23:53,130
These are very common business phrases.

512
00:23:53,130 --> 00:23:56,410
Let's make this more real with a short role play.

513
00:23:56,410 --> 00:23:57,410
Great idea.

514
00:23:57,410 --> 00:23:59,010
This will help our listeners practice.

515
00:23:59,010 --> 00:24:00,010
Hi.

516
00:24:00,010 --> 00:24:01,010
Nice to meet you.

517
00:24:01,010 --> 00:24:02,210
What do you do?

518
00:24:02,210 --> 00:24:03,370
Nice to meet you too.

519
00:24:03,370 --> 00:24:04,850
I'm a business analyst.

520
00:24:04,850 --> 00:24:09,090
I analyze data and help companies improve their performance.

521
00:24:09,090 --> 00:24:10,250
That sounds interesting.

522
00:24:10,250 --> 00:24:11,530
Where do you work?

523
00:24:11,530 --> 00:24:13,230
I work at a consulting firm.

524
00:24:13,230 --> 00:24:16,190
We work with different clients across industries.

525
00:24:16,190 --> 00:24:16,870
Great.

526
00:24:16,870 --> 00:24:19,230
What are your main responsibilities?

527
00:24:19,230 --> 00:24:22,270
I'm responsible for analyzing business processes,

528
00:24:22,270 --> 00:24:25,030
preparing reports, and presenting recommendations

529
00:24:25,030 --> 00:24:26,230
to clients.

530
00:24:26,230 --> 00:24:28,630
Do you work alone or with a team?

531
00:24:28,630 --> 00:24:29,670
I work with a team.

532
00:24:29,670 --> 00:24:32,270
We collaborate closely on projects.

533
00:24:32,270 --> 00:24:34,390
How long have you been doing this?

534
00:24:34,390 --> 00:24:37,630
I've been working in this field for about six years.

535
00:24:37,630 --> 00:24:39,310
Do you enjoy your job?

536
00:24:39,310 --> 00:24:40,270
Yes, I do.

537
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:43,610
I enjoy solving problems and working with clients.

538
00:24:43,610 --> 00:24:45,590
That was a great example.

539
00:24:45,590 --> 00:24:50,070
Yes, and notice how we used simple but professional language.

540
00:24:50,070 --> 00:24:53,110
Now let's talk about talking about your goals.

541
00:24:53,110 --> 00:24:56,150
Yes, this often comes up in conversations.

542
00:24:56,150 --> 00:24:59,810
You can say, I'm looking to, for example,

543
00:24:59,810 --> 00:25:02,810
I'm looking to develop my leadership skills,

544
00:25:02,810 --> 00:25:06,330
or I want to move into a management role.

545
00:25:06,330 --> 00:25:08,990
Or I'm working towards a promotion.

546
00:25:08,990 --> 00:25:11,070
Very useful phrases.

547
00:25:11,070 --> 00:25:14,070
Now let's talk about common mistakes.

548
00:25:14,070 --> 00:25:16,470
Yes, this is very important.

549
00:25:16,470 --> 00:25:20,310
Mistake one, saying, I am engineer.

550
00:25:20,310 --> 00:25:23,670
Correct is I am an engineer.

551
00:25:23,670 --> 00:25:27,190
Mistake two, I work in Google.

552
00:25:27,190 --> 00:25:31,790
Correct, I work at Google or I work for Google.

553
00:25:31,790 --> 00:25:35,430
Mistake three, I am experienced.

554
00:25:35,430 --> 00:25:38,350
Correct, I am experienced.

555
00:25:38,350 --> 00:25:41,750
These small mistakes make a big difference.

556
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:43,590
Let's do a quick practice.

557
00:25:43,590 --> 00:25:45,670
I'll ask you answer.

558
00:25:45,670 --> 00:25:46,550
OK.

559
00:25:46,550 --> 00:25:47,990
What do you do?

560
00:25:47,990 --> 00:25:49,910
I'm a project coordinator.

561
00:25:49,910 --> 00:25:53,270
I organize tasks and support the project team.

562
00:25:53,270 --> 00:25:54,790
Where do you work?

563
00:25:54,790 --> 00:25:56,630
I work at an international company

564
00:25:56,630 --> 00:25:58,510
in the logistics industry.

565
00:25:58,510 --> 00:26:00,750
What are your responsibilities?

566
00:26:00,750 --> 00:26:03,430
I'm responsible for scheduling, communication,

567
00:26:03,430 --> 00:26:04,790
and reporting.

568
00:26:04,790 --> 00:26:05,950
Excellent.

569
00:26:05,950 --> 00:26:08,390
Before we finish, let's summarize.

570
00:26:08,390 --> 00:26:11,390
First, introduce your job clearly.

571
00:26:11,390 --> 00:26:13,990
Second, explain what you do.

572
00:26:13,990 --> 00:26:16,510
Third, talk about where you work.

573
00:26:16,510 --> 00:26:20,510
Fourth, describe your responsibilities and experience.

574
00:26:20,510 --> 00:26:24,310
And finally, keep your language simple and clear.

575
00:26:24,310 --> 00:26:27,150
Now it's time for our question of the day.

576
00:26:27,150 --> 00:26:31,110
What do you do and how would you describe your job in English?

577
00:26:31,110 --> 00:26:33,590
Write your answer and practice using the phrases

578
00:26:33,590 --> 00:26:35,150
we learned today.

579
00:26:35,150 --> 00:26:37,550
Thank you so much for joining us.

580
00:26:37,550 --> 00:26:39,430
Keep practicing, keep speaking,

581
00:26:39,430 --> 00:26:42,070
and keep improving your business English.

582
00:26:42,070 --> 00:26:44,150
We'll see you in the next episode.

583
00:26:44,150 --> 00:26:45,330
Goodbye, everyone.

584
00:26:45,330 --> 00:26:49,140
Goodbye.

585
00:26:49,140 --> 00:26:50,260
Hello, everyone.

586
00:26:50,260 --> 00:26:52,620
We're really happy to have you with us today.

587
00:26:52,620 --> 00:26:53,460
Hi, everyone.

588
00:26:53,460 --> 00:26:54,860
Thanks for joining us.

589
00:26:54,860 --> 00:26:56,940
If you're here to improve your English,

590
00:26:56,940 --> 00:26:58,780
you're in the right place.

591
00:26:58,780 --> 00:26:59,780
I'm Emma.

592
00:26:59,780 --> 00:27:00,980
And I'm Jack.

593
00:27:00,980 --> 00:27:04,580
On this channel, we help you speak clear, natural English

594
00:27:04,580 --> 00:27:07,860
with confidence in real business situations.

595
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:12,500
If you enjoy this lesson, please give us a thumbs up, and don't forget to subscribe.

596
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:15,100
Yes, your support helps us so much.

597
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:16,460
Thank you for being here.

598
00:27:16,460 --> 00:27:18,900
So Emma, what are we talking about today?

599
00:27:18,900 --> 00:27:21,540
Today we have a very practical topic.

600
00:27:21,540 --> 00:27:25,380
We're going to learn how to talk about your job in business English.

601
00:27:25,380 --> 00:27:27,420
This is such an important skill.

602
00:27:27,420 --> 00:27:31,620
Whether you're in a meeting, a job interview, or a networking event, you need to explain

603
00:27:31,620 --> 00:27:33,300
your job clearly.

604
00:27:33,300 --> 00:27:34,460
Exactly.

605
00:27:34,460 --> 00:27:40,100
And today, we'll make it simple, natural, and very practical with real examples.

606
00:27:40,100 --> 00:27:41,100
Sounds perfect.

607
00:27:41,100 --> 00:27:43,180
Before we start, how are you feeling today?

608
00:27:43,180 --> 00:27:44,420
I'm feeling great.

609
00:27:44,420 --> 00:27:47,700
I'm excited because this is something everyone needs.

610
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:48,700
How about you?

611
00:27:48,700 --> 00:27:49,700
I'm doing well.

612
00:27:49,700 --> 00:27:53,100
I think this lesson will help a lot of people feel more confident.

613
00:27:53,100 --> 00:27:54,100
I agree.

614
00:27:54,100 --> 00:27:56,580
Okay, everyone, let's get started.

615
00:27:56,580 --> 00:27:59,420
Let's begin with the most common question.

616
00:27:59,420 --> 00:28:04,060
When you meet someone in a business situation, how do you ask about their job?

617
00:28:04,060 --> 00:28:07,340
The most common question is, what do you do?

618
00:28:07,340 --> 00:28:08,940
Very simple and natural.

619
00:28:08,940 --> 00:28:12,740
Yes, you can also say, what do you do for a living?

620
00:28:12,740 --> 00:28:15,420
That sounds slightly more formal, right?

621
00:28:15,420 --> 00:28:17,700
Exactly, but both are correct.

622
00:28:17,700 --> 00:28:19,820
So how do you answer that question?

623
00:28:19,820 --> 00:28:24,420
The simplest way is to say, I'm a plus your job title.

624
00:28:24,420 --> 00:28:25,420
For example?

625
00:28:25,420 --> 00:28:27,300
I'm a project manager.

626
00:28:27,300 --> 00:28:29,380
Or I'm a software engineer.

627
00:28:29,380 --> 00:28:30,380
Perfect.

628
00:28:30,380 --> 00:28:32,380
Then you can add more details.

629
00:28:32,380 --> 00:28:34,060
Let's give a practical example.

630
00:28:34,060 --> 00:28:35,060
Sure.

631
00:28:35,060 --> 00:28:36,520
I'm a marketing specialist.

632
00:28:36,520 --> 00:28:41,020
I manage social media campaigns and analyze customer data.

633
00:28:41,020 --> 00:28:42,580
That's very clear.

634
00:28:42,580 --> 00:28:43,660
Another example.

635
00:28:43,660 --> 00:28:44,740
I'm an accountant.

636
00:28:44,740 --> 00:28:48,540
I prepare financial reports and manage company budgets.

637
00:28:48,540 --> 00:28:49,540
I like that.

638
00:28:49,540 --> 00:28:51,460
It's simple but professional.

639
00:28:51,460 --> 00:28:52,460
Exactly.

640
00:28:52,460 --> 00:28:56,260
Always try to add what you do, not just your title.

641
00:28:56,260 --> 00:28:59,340
Because job titles alone are sometimes not enough.

642
00:28:59,340 --> 00:29:00,340
Right.

643
00:29:00,340 --> 00:29:03,060
For example, I'm a business analyst.

644
00:29:03,060 --> 00:29:06,900
I work with data to help companies make better decisions.

645
00:29:06,900 --> 00:29:09,140
That explains the value of the job.

646
00:29:09,140 --> 00:29:12,860
Yes, and that's very important in business English.

647
00:29:12,860 --> 00:29:15,540
Now let's talk about where you work.

648
00:29:15,540 --> 00:29:16,540
Good idea.

649
00:29:16,540 --> 00:29:18,860
This is another common question.

650
00:29:18,860 --> 00:29:21,120
Someone might ask, where do you work?

651
00:29:21,120 --> 00:29:24,900
You can say, I work at, or I work for.

652
00:29:24,900 --> 00:29:26,400
What's the difference?

653
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:28,300
At is for a place.

654
00:29:28,300 --> 00:29:30,120
For is for a company.

655
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:31,440
Give us an example.

656
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:33,240
I work at a bank.

657
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:35,480
And I work for HSBC.

658
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:36,680
Exactly.

659
00:29:36,680 --> 00:29:39,280
You can also say, I work in.

660
00:29:39,280 --> 00:29:41,200
When do we use in?

661
00:29:41,200 --> 00:29:43,760
For industries or environments.

662
00:29:43,760 --> 00:29:46,560
For example, I work in finance.

663
00:29:46,560 --> 00:29:48,360
That's very useful.

664
00:29:48,360 --> 00:29:51,800
Another example, I work in the healthcare industry.

665
00:29:51,800 --> 00:29:52,840
Nice.

666
00:29:52,840 --> 00:29:55,640
You can also say, I work from home.

667
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:57,360
That's very common now.

668
00:29:57,360 --> 00:29:58,360
Yes.

669
00:29:58,360 --> 00:30:00,000
Or I work remotely.

670
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,160
Let's build a full answer.

671
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:04,840
Sure, I'm a software developer.

672
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:08,520
I work for a tech company and I mostly work from home.

673
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:10,480
That's a perfect answer.

674
00:30:10,480 --> 00:30:14,080
Now let's talk about describing your responsibilities.

675
00:30:14,080 --> 00:30:17,000
This is where you really show your English skills.

676
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:18,160
Exactly.

677
00:30:18,160 --> 00:30:21,960
You can say, my main responsibility is to...

678
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:23,280
For example?

679
00:30:23,280 --> 00:30:27,240
My main responsibility is to manage client accounts.

680
00:30:27,240 --> 00:30:28,080
Good.

681
00:30:28,080 --> 00:30:35,080
Or, my responsibilities include organizing meetings, preparing reports, and communicating with clients.

682
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:36,780
That's very professional.

683
00:30:36,780 --> 00:30:38,580
Let's give more examples.

684
00:30:38,580 --> 00:30:39,380
Okay.

685
00:30:39,380 --> 00:30:41,480
I work in customer service.

686
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:44,880
I handle customer inquiries and resolve complaints.

687
00:30:44,880 --> 00:30:45,980
That's clear.

688
00:30:45,980 --> 00:30:47,780
I'm a sales executive.

689
00:30:47,780 --> 00:30:51,580
I meet clients, present products, and close deals.

690
00:30:51,580 --> 00:30:53,880
That sounds very business-focused.

691
00:30:53,880 --> 00:30:55,080
Exactly.

692
00:30:55,080 --> 00:30:57,780
So what about someone in HR?

693
00:30:57,780 --> 00:31:00,420
Good example, I work in HR.

694
00:31:00,420 --> 00:31:04,180
I recruit new employees and manage training programs.

695
00:31:04,180 --> 00:31:05,140
Nice.

696
00:31:05,140 --> 00:31:09,060
The key is to use simple verbs like manage, organize,

697
00:31:09,060 --> 00:31:11,540
create, analyze, support.

698
00:31:11,540 --> 00:31:13,460
Simple, but effective.

699
00:31:13,460 --> 00:31:16,900
Now let's talk about your daily routine at work.

700
00:31:16,900 --> 00:31:18,780
That's another common topic.

701
00:31:18,780 --> 00:31:21,580
You can describe your day step by step.

702
00:31:21,580 --> 00:31:22,980
Give us an example.

703
00:31:22,980 --> 00:31:25,340
I start my day by checking emails.

704
00:31:25,340 --> 00:31:27,280
Then I attend meetings.

705
00:31:27,280 --> 00:31:30,040
After that, I work on my main tasks.

706
00:31:30,040 --> 00:31:32,640
In the afternoon, I collaborate with my team.

707
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:34,920
That's very clear and structured.

708
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:37,520
Yes, structure helps a lot.

709
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:38,760
Let me try one.

710
00:31:38,760 --> 00:31:39,760
Go ahead.

711
00:31:39,760 --> 00:31:42,320
I usually start work at 9.

712
00:31:42,320 --> 00:31:45,760
First I review my tasks, then I work on projects.

713
00:31:45,760 --> 00:31:48,400
In the afternoon, I have calls with clients.

714
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:50,160
I finish around 6.

715
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:51,160
Perfect.

716
00:31:51,160 --> 00:31:53,000
That's exactly how to do it.

717
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:55,360
Now let's talk about who you work with.

718
00:31:55,360 --> 00:31:57,800
Yes, your team and colleagues.

719
00:31:57,800 --> 00:32:01,760
You can say, I work with a team of, for example,

720
00:32:01,760 --> 00:32:04,700
I work with a team of five engineers.

721
00:32:04,700 --> 00:32:07,640
Or I collaborate with different departments.

722
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:09,560
That sounds very professional.

723
00:32:09,560 --> 00:32:11,120
What about your boss?

724
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:14,600
You can say, I report to the marketing manager.

725
00:32:14,600 --> 00:32:15,680
Good phrase.

726
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:18,520
Or I work under the sales director.

727
00:32:18,520 --> 00:32:19,820
That's also common.

728
00:32:19,820 --> 00:32:22,080
If you are the boss, you can say,

729
00:32:22,080 --> 00:32:24,660
I manage a team of 10 people.

730
00:32:24,660 --> 00:32:26,320
That shows leadership.

731
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:29,280
Now let's talk about what you like about your job.

732
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:32,520
This is important in interviews and conversations.

733
00:32:32,520 --> 00:32:36,140
You can say, I enjoy, for example,

734
00:32:36,140 --> 00:32:38,360
I enjoy working with my team.

735
00:32:38,360 --> 00:32:39,280
Nice.

736
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:41,440
I enjoy solving problems.

737
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:42,640
That sounds good.

738
00:32:42,640 --> 00:32:45,800
Or I love the flexibility of my job.

739
00:32:45,800 --> 00:32:47,400
That's very modern.

740
00:32:47,400 --> 00:32:51,080
You can also say, I find my job rewarding.

741
00:32:51,080 --> 00:32:52,760
That's a great phrase.

742
00:32:52,760 --> 00:32:55,000
Now what about challenges?

743
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:58,280
Yes, how do we talk about them professionally?

744
00:32:58,280 --> 00:33:00,240
Use soft language.

745
00:33:00,240 --> 00:33:04,040
For example, sometimes the workload can be heavy.

746
00:33:04,040 --> 00:33:05,520
That sounds polite.

747
00:33:05,520 --> 00:33:08,840
Or managing deadlines can be challenging.

748
00:33:08,840 --> 00:33:10,400
Very professional.

749
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:14,560
Avoid strong negative words like, I hate my job.

750
00:33:14,560 --> 00:33:17,320
Yes, especially in business settings.

751
00:33:17,320 --> 00:33:19,440
Now let's do a role play.

752
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:20,600
Great idea.

753
00:33:20,600 --> 00:33:21,720
I'll start.

754
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:23,320
Hi, nice to meet you.

755
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:24,440
Nice to meet you too.

756
00:33:24,440 --> 00:33:25,560
What do you do?

757
00:33:25,560 --> 00:33:27,400
I'm a financial analyst.

758
00:33:27,400 --> 00:33:29,460
I work for an investment firm.

759
00:33:29,460 --> 00:33:30,640
That sounds interesting.

760
00:33:30,640 --> 00:33:32,120
What do you do exactly?

761
00:33:32,120 --> 00:33:36,080
I analyze market trends and prepare reports for clients.

762
00:33:36,080 --> 00:33:37,280
That's impressive.

763
00:33:37,280 --> 00:33:38,760
Do you enjoy your job?

764
00:33:38,760 --> 00:33:41,120
Yes, I really enjoy working with data

765
00:33:41,120 --> 00:33:42,640
and solving problems.

766
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:43,600
That's great.

767
00:33:43,600 --> 00:33:44,800
Now your turn.

768
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:45,640
Okay.

769
00:33:45,640 --> 00:33:46,840
Hi, I'm Jack.

770
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:48,440
I'm a project manager.

771
00:33:48,440 --> 00:33:49,640
Nice to meet you.

772
00:33:49,640 --> 00:33:52,080
What do you do as a project manager?

773
00:33:52,080 --> 00:33:54,600
I manage projects, coordinate teams,

774
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:57,400
and make sure everything is delivered on time.

775
00:33:57,400 --> 00:33:59,760
That sounds like a lot of responsibility.

776
00:33:59,760 --> 00:34:02,840
Yes, it can be challenging, but I enjoy it.

777
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:03,680
Perfect.

778
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:05,480
That felt very natural.

779
00:34:05,480 --> 00:34:07,480
Yes, and very practical.

780
00:34:07,480 --> 00:34:10,000
Now let's talk about career goals.

781
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:11,600
Another important topic.

782
00:34:11,600 --> 00:34:13,000
Someone might ask,

783
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:15,440
where do you see yourself in the future?

784
00:34:15,440 --> 00:34:17,520
You can say, I'd like to.

785
00:34:17,520 --> 00:34:21,280
For example, I'd like to become a senior manager.

786
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:24,520
Or I want to develop my skills in leadership.

787
00:34:24,520 --> 00:34:25,800
That's excellent.

788
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:29,200
You can also say I'm working towards a promotion.

789
00:34:29,200 --> 00:34:31,360
Yes, very professional.

790
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:34,200
Now let's talk about common mistakes.

791
00:34:34,200 --> 00:34:36,120
This is very important.

792
00:34:36,120 --> 00:34:39,240
Mistake one, I am engineer.

793
00:34:39,240 --> 00:34:41,920
Correct is I am an engineer.

794
00:34:41,920 --> 00:34:45,080
Mistake two, I work in Google.

795
00:34:45,080 --> 00:34:49,080
Correct is, I work at Google or I work for Google.

796
00:34:49,080 --> 00:34:52,280
Mistake three, I am experienced.

797
00:34:52,280 --> 00:34:54,780
Correct is, I am experienced.

798
00:34:54,780 --> 00:34:58,740
These small mistakes can change how professional you sound.

799
00:34:58,740 --> 00:35:00,000
Exactly.

800
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:02,040
Let's do a quick practice.

801
00:35:02,040 --> 00:35:04,520
Okay, I work in a hospital.

802
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:05,360
Correct.

803
00:35:05,360 --> 00:35:06,680
I am a teacher.

804
00:35:06,680 --> 00:35:07,520
Correct.

805
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:09,640
I am very experienced.

806
00:35:09,640 --> 00:35:12,440
Incorrect, it should be experienced.

807
00:35:12,440 --> 00:35:13,280
Great.

808
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:15,880
Now let's do one final role play.

809
00:35:15,880 --> 00:35:16,720
Okay.

810
00:35:16,720 --> 00:35:18,300
Tell me about your job.

811
00:35:18,300 --> 00:35:19,680
I'm a digital marketer.

812
00:35:19,680 --> 00:35:21,800
I work for an online company.

813
00:35:21,800 --> 00:35:23,120
What do you do there?

814
00:35:23,120 --> 00:35:24,920
I create marketing campaigns

815
00:35:24,920 --> 00:35:27,160
and analyze performance data.

816
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:28,720
Do you enjoy your job?

817
00:35:28,720 --> 00:35:30,800
Yes, I enjoy the creative aspect

818
00:35:30,800 --> 00:35:32,500
and working with data.

819
00:35:32,500 --> 00:35:34,240
What are your future goals?

820
00:35:34,240 --> 00:35:36,600
I'd like to become a marketing manager.

821
00:35:36,600 --> 00:35:37,820
Excellent answer.

822
00:35:37,820 --> 00:35:39,320
That was very useful.

823
00:35:39,320 --> 00:35:41,520
Yes, and very realistic.

824
00:35:41,520 --> 00:35:42,720
Let's wrap up.

825
00:35:42,720 --> 00:35:47,280
Today, we learned how to talk about your job clearly and confidently.

826
00:35:47,280 --> 00:35:48,780
Use simple phrases.

827
00:35:48,780 --> 00:35:50,540
Be clear and natural.

828
00:35:50,540 --> 00:35:52,740
Add details about what you do.

829
00:35:52,740 --> 00:35:54,620
And practice regularly.

830
00:35:54,620 --> 00:35:56,120
Now it's your turn.

831
00:35:56,120 --> 00:35:57,420
What do you do?

832
