850
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:01,440
English.

851
00:37:01,440 --> 00:37:03,480
That's such a useful topic.

852
00:37:03,480 --> 00:37:08,360
Whether you're in a meeting, a job interview, or just networking, you need to talk about

853
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:11,160
your job clearly and confidently.

854
00:37:11,160 --> 00:37:12,160
Exactly.

855
00:37:12,160 --> 00:37:14,700
And today, we're going to go much deeper.

856
00:37:14,700 --> 00:37:19,120
We'll give you real examples, useful phrases, and natural conversations.

857
00:37:19,120 --> 00:37:21,920
Yes, and everything will be practical.

858
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:23,840
No complicated theory.

859
00:37:23,840 --> 00:37:26,920
Just real English you can use immediately.

860
00:37:26,920 --> 00:37:28,080
Sounds great.

861
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:32,560
So Emily, let's start with the most basic question people ask about jobs.

862
00:37:32,560 --> 00:37:33,560
Of course.

863
00:37:33,560 --> 00:37:36,760
The most common question is, what do you do?

864
00:37:36,760 --> 00:37:39,400
Simple, short, and very natural.

865
00:37:39,400 --> 00:37:40,400
Yes.

866
00:37:40,400 --> 00:37:43,000
Many learners say, what is your job?

867
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:49,020
Which is okay, but what do you do sounds much more natural in everyday conversation.

868
00:37:49,020 --> 00:37:51,100
So how do we answer that question?

869
00:37:51,100 --> 00:37:55,860
The easiest way is, I'm a plus your job title.

870
00:37:55,860 --> 00:37:58,700
For example, I'm a project manager.

871
00:37:58,700 --> 00:38:01,420
Or I'm a software engineer.

872
00:38:01,420 --> 00:38:03,220
Or I'm an accountant.

873
00:38:03,220 --> 00:38:04,300
Exactly.

874
00:38:04,300 --> 00:38:07,900
And if you want to sound more professional, you can add more detail.

875
00:38:07,900 --> 00:38:10,900
For example, I'm a project manager.

876
00:38:10,900 --> 00:38:14,900
I manage cross-functional teams and deliver projects on time.

877
00:38:14,900 --> 00:38:18,900
That already sounds much stronger than just saying your job title.

878
00:38:18,900 --> 00:38:20,900
Let's give a few more real-world examples.

879
00:38:20,900 --> 00:38:23,900
Sure. I'm a marketing specialist.

880
00:38:23,900 --> 00:38:27,900
I focus on digital campaigns and customer engagement.

881
00:38:27,900 --> 00:38:29,900
I'm a customer service representative.

882
00:38:29,900 --> 00:38:32,900
I handle client inquiries and resolve issues.

883
00:38:32,900 --> 00:38:34,900
I'm a data analyst.

884
00:38:34,900 --> 00:38:40,060
I analyze data and create reports to support business decisions.

885
00:38:40,060 --> 00:38:41,860
Notice something important here.

886
00:38:41,860 --> 00:38:46,940
Yes, these sentences are simple but very clear and professional.

887
00:38:46,940 --> 00:38:49,660
Now let's go one step further.

888
00:38:49,660 --> 00:38:52,900
Sometimes people ask, can you tell me more about your role?

889
00:38:52,900 --> 00:38:53,900
Good point.

890
00:38:53,900 --> 00:38:56,740
This is where you explain your responsibilities.

891
00:38:56,740 --> 00:38:58,140
So how can we do that?

892
00:38:58,140 --> 00:39:04,700
You can say, my main responsibility is or I'm responsible for X.

893
00:39:04,700 --> 00:39:10,540
For example, I'm responsible for managing client accounts and maintaining relationships.

894
00:39:10,540 --> 00:39:16,980
Or my main responsibility is to oversee project timelines and ensure delivery.

895
00:39:16,980 --> 00:39:20,620
That already sounds much stronger than just saying your job title.

896
00:39:20,620 --> 00:39:23,300
Let's give a few more real-world examples.

897
00:39:23,300 --> 00:39:25,780
Sure, I'm a team leader.

898
00:39:25,780 --> 00:39:30,620
I manage a group of five people and I'm responsible for planning projects and tracking

899
00:39:30,620 --> 00:39:31,620
progress.

900
00:39:31,620 --> 00:39:35,060
That's excellent. Clear structure and easy to understand.

901
00:39:35,060 --> 00:39:37,380
Now let's talk about where you work.

902
00:39:37,380 --> 00:39:40,180
Yes, this is another very common question.

903
00:39:40,180 --> 00:39:41,460
Where do you work?

904
00:39:41,460 --> 00:39:43,660
You can answer in different ways.

905
00:39:43,660 --> 00:39:46,420
For example, I work at Amazon.

906
00:39:46,420 --> 00:39:49,820
Or I work for a multinational company.

907
00:39:49,820 --> 00:39:52,540
Or I work in the finance industry.

908
00:39:52,540 --> 00:39:54,940
Let's clarify something important.

909
00:39:54,940 --> 00:39:57,860
Yes, because many learners make mistakes here.

910
00:39:57,860 --> 00:40:04,980
We say work at for a place, work for for a company, and work in for an industry.

911
00:40:04,980 --> 00:40:12,980
Exactly. For example, I work at a hospital. I work for a healthcare company. I work in the medical field.

912
00:40:12,980 --> 00:40:18,900
Now let's talk about daily tasks. This is where you describe what you actually do every day.

913
00:40:18,900 --> 00:40:22,340
Yes, this is very important in business communication.

914
00:40:22,340 --> 00:40:25,460
You can say, on a typical day, I...

915
00:40:25,460 --> 00:40:31,460
For example, on a typical day, I check emails, attend meetings, and coordinate with my team.

916
00:40:31,460 --> 00:40:36,660
Or I spend most of my time analyzing data and preparing reports.

917
00:40:36,660 --> 00:40:38,820
Let's give a more detailed example.

918
00:40:38,820 --> 00:40:46,180
Sure. I start my day by reviewing my emails and setting priorities. Then I attend team meetings.

919
00:40:46,180 --> 00:40:50,580
In the afternoon, I focus on project work and client communication.

920
00:40:50,580 --> 00:40:53,300
That sounds very professional and structured.

921
00:40:53,300 --> 00:40:56,340
Now, let's talk about talking about your team.

922
00:40:56,340 --> 00:40:59,500
Yes, this is common in meetings and introductions.

923
00:40:59,500 --> 00:41:02,540
You can say, I work with a team of...

924
00:41:02,540 --> 00:41:06,860
For example, I work with a team of engineers and designers.

925
00:41:06,860 --> 00:41:11,340
Or, I collaborate closely with the sales and marketing teams.

926
00:41:11,340 --> 00:41:12,780
And if you're a manager...

927
00:41:12,780 --> 00:41:16,180
You can say, I manage a team of 10 people.

928
00:41:16,180 --> 00:41:20,020
Or, I lead a department focused on product development.

929
00:41:20,020 --> 00:41:22,500
Now, let's talk about achievements.

930
00:41:22,500 --> 00:41:26,380
This is very useful in interviews and performance discussions.

931
00:41:26,380 --> 00:41:28,820
Yes, this is where you show your value.

932
00:41:28,820 --> 00:41:31,860
You can say, I recently completed...

933
00:41:31,860 --> 00:41:35,380
For example, I recently completed a major project

934
00:41:35,380 --> 00:41:36,660
ahead of schedule.

935
00:41:36,660 --> 00:41:41,060
Or I helped increase sales by 20% last quarter.

936
00:41:41,060 --> 00:41:42,700
Let's make it more natural.

937
00:41:42,700 --> 00:41:45,260
Sure, one of my key achievements

938
00:41:45,260 --> 00:41:47,840
was improving our customer response time.

939
00:41:47,840 --> 00:41:49,980
That sounds strong and confident.

940
00:41:49,980 --> 00:41:52,420
Now let's talk about challenges.

941
00:41:52,420 --> 00:41:55,340
Yes, because every job has challenges.

942
00:41:55,340 --> 00:41:58,420
You can say, one challenge I face is...

943
00:41:58,420 --> 00:42:00,780
For example, one challenge I face

944
00:42:00,780 --> 00:42:02,780
is managing tight deadlines,

945
00:42:02,780 --> 00:42:06,680
or it can be difficult to balance multiple priorities.

946
00:42:06,680 --> 00:42:09,020
Notice how we keep the tone professional.

947
00:42:09,020 --> 00:42:12,460
Yes, we don't complain, we explain.

948
00:42:12,460 --> 00:42:15,180
Now let's talk about job satisfaction.

949
00:42:15,180 --> 00:42:17,900
This is very common in conversations.

950
00:42:17,900 --> 00:42:20,420
Someone might ask, do you like your job?

951
00:42:20,420 --> 00:42:23,340
You can say, yes, I really enjoy it.

952
00:42:23,340 --> 00:42:25,740
Or, I find it very rewarding.

953
00:42:25,740 --> 00:42:27,980
And if you want to explain why,

954
00:42:27,980 --> 00:42:31,100
I enjoy working with my team and solving problems.

955
00:42:31,100 --> 00:42:34,820
Or, I like the challenges and opportunities to learn.

956
00:42:34,820 --> 00:42:36,940
And if you don't fully enjoy it,

957
00:42:36,940 --> 00:42:39,340
you can say, it has its challenges,

958
00:42:39,340 --> 00:42:40,620
but I'm learning a lot.

959
00:42:40,620 --> 00:42:42,720
That's a very professional answer.

960
00:42:42,720 --> 00:42:46,500
Now let's move into a realistic conversation example.

961
00:42:46,500 --> 00:42:47,460
Great idea.

962
00:42:47,460 --> 00:42:49,140
Hi, nice to meet you.

963
00:42:49,140 --> 00:42:50,180
What do you do?

964
00:42:50,180 --> 00:42:51,580
Nice to meet you too.

965
00:42:51,580 --> 00:42:53,100
I'm a business analyst.

966
00:42:53,100 --> 00:42:54,740
I work for a consulting firm.

967
00:42:54,740 --> 00:42:55,660
How about you?

968
00:42:55,660 --> 00:42:57,780
I'm a human resources manager.

969
00:42:57,780 --> 00:43:00,860
I handle recruitment and employee relations.

970
00:43:00,860 --> 00:43:02,220
That sounds interesting.

971
00:43:02,220 --> 00:43:04,160
What does your typical day look like?

972
00:43:04,160 --> 00:43:06,300
I usually start with emails,

973
00:43:06,300 --> 00:43:08,500
then I have interviews or meetings.

974
00:43:08,500 --> 00:43:11,500
In the afternoon, I focus on HR strategies

975
00:43:11,500 --> 00:43:12,780
and team support.

976
00:43:12,780 --> 00:43:13,820
That's great.

977
00:43:13,820 --> 00:43:16,320
I mostly work with data and reports.

978
00:43:16,320 --> 00:43:19,660
I analyze business performance and provide insights.

979
00:43:19,660 --> 00:43:22,280
That's a very natural conversation.

980
00:43:22,280 --> 00:43:25,340
Yes, and it uses simple, practical English.

981
00:43:25,340 --> 00:43:27,780
Let's do a more advanced example.

982
00:43:27,780 --> 00:43:28,620
Okay.

983
00:43:28,620 --> 00:43:31,060
Can you tell me about your role in more detail?

984
00:43:31,060 --> 00:43:31,980
Sure.

985
00:43:31,980 --> 00:43:33,980
I'm a senior project manager.

986
00:43:33,980 --> 00:43:36,980
I oversee multiple projects, coordinate teams,

987
00:43:36,980 --> 00:43:39,540
and ensure everything is delivered on time

988
00:43:39,540 --> 00:43:40,700
and within budget.

989
00:43:40,700 --> 00:43:42,060
That's impressive.

990
00:43:42,060 --> 00:43:44,600
What's the most challenging part of your job?

991
00:43:44,600 --> 00:43:47,040
Managing expectations and tight deadlines

992
00:43:47,040 --> 00:43:50,040
can be challenging, but I enjoy problem solving.

993
00:43:50,040 --> 00:43:53,040
Excellent. That's very professional English.

994
00:43:53,040 --> 00:43:55,440
Now let's talk about career goals.

995
00:43:55,440 --> 00:43:58,080
Yes, this is common in interviews.

996
00:43:58,080 --> 00:44:00,280
You can say, I'd like to.

997
00:44:00,280 --> 00:44:03,800
For example, I'd like to move into a leadership role.

998
00:44:03,800 --> 00:44:07,800
Or I want to develop my skills in strategy and management.

999
00:44:07,800 --> 00:44:11,120
Now let's do a quick role play for a job interview.

1000
00:44:11,120 --> 00:44:11,840
Perfect.

1001
00:44:11,840 --> 00:44:13,640
Can you tell me about yourself?

1002
00:44:13,640 --> 00:44:15,840
Sure. I'm a marketing professional

1003
00:44:15,840 --> 00:44:18,220
with over five years of experience.

1004
00:44:18,220 --> 00:44:21,820
I specialize in digital marketing and campaign management.

1005
00:44:21,820 --> 00:44:25,040
What are your main responsibilities in your current role?

1006
00:44:25,040 --> 00:44:28,720
I manage online campaigns, analyze performance data,

1007
00:44:28,720 --> 00:44:32,080
and work with cross-functional teams to improve results.

1008
00:44:32,080 --> 00:44:34,400
Why are you looking for a new opportunity?

1009
00:44:34,400 --> 00:44:36,840
I'm looking for new challenges and opportunities

1010
00:44:36,840 --> 00:44:38,320
to grow professionally.

1011
00:44:38,320 --> 00:44:40,880
That's a strong and clear response.

1012
00:44:40,880 --> 00:44:43,240
Now let's wrap up with key tips.

1013
00:44:43,240 --> 00:44:46,520
First, keep your language simple and clear.

1014
00:44:46,520 --> 00:44:50,800
Second, always add a little detail, not just your job title.

1015
00:44:50,800 --> 00:44:54,520
Third, use real examples to explain your work.

1016
00:44:54,520 --> 00:44:56,920
Fourth, practice speaking out loud.

1017
00:44:56,920 --> 00:45:00,000
And most importantly, be confident.

1018
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:02,040
Your English doesn't need to be perfect,

1019
00:45:02,040 --> 00:45:03,880
just clear and natural.

1020
00:45:03,880 --> 00:45:06,040
So now it's your turn.

1021
00:45:06,040 --> 00:45:07,840
Try answering this question.

1022
00:45:07,840 --> 00:45:08,920
What do you do?

1023
00:45:08,920 --> 00:45:12,800
Add your job, your responsibilities, and one example.

1024
00:45:12,800 --> 00:45:15,120
Practice it until it feels natural.

