You can, but it sounds a bit formal.

1079
00:46:59,200 --> 00:47:02,040
Native speakers usually say, what do you do?

1080
00:47:02,040 --> 00:47:02,880
Got it.

1081
00:47:02,880 --> 00:47:05,200
So what do you do is the best choice.

1082
00:47:05,200 --> 00:47:07,360
Now, how do I answer this question?

1083
00:47:07,360 --> 00:47:11,560
The simplest way is to say I'm a plus your job title.

1084
00:47:11,560 --> 00:47:13,440
For example, I'm a teacher.

1085
00:47:13,440 --> 00:47:16,960
So I would say I'm a manager or I'm an engineer.

1086
00:47:16,960 --> 00:47:17,840
Perfect.

1087
00:47:17,840 --> 00:47:19,880
You can also add more details.

1088
00:47:19,880 --> 00:47:21,680
For example, I'm a teacher.

1089
00:47:21,680 --> 00:47:23,800
I teach English to adults.

1090
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:24,480
I like that.

1091
00:47:24,480 --> 00:47:27,960
So first you say your job, then you explain a little more.

1092
00:47:27,960 --> 00:47:29,000
Exactly.

1093
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:31,360
Let me give you some practical examples.

1094
00:47:31,360 --> 00:47:32,200
I'm a nurse.

1095
00:47:32,200 --> 00:47:33,640
I work in a hospital.

1096
00:47:33,640 --> 00:47:34,840
Or I'm a chef.

1097
00:47:34,840 --> 00:47:36,560
I run a small restaurant.

1098
00:47:36,560 --> 00:47:38,000
Those are great examples.

1099
00:47:38,000 --> 00:47:39,240
Let me try one.

1100
00:47:39,240 --> 00:47:40,680
I'm a sales executive.

1101
00:47:40,680 --> 00:47:42,440
I work for an international company

1102
00:47:42,440 --> 00:47:44,520
and handle client relationships.

1103
00:47:44,520 --> 00:47:45,200
Excellent.

1104
00:47:45,200 --> 00:47:47,120
That sounds very professional.

1105
00:47:47,120 --> 00:47:49,560
What if someone doesn't have a job right now?

1106
00:47:49,560 --> 00:47:52,280
You can say I'm currently looking for a job

1107
00:47:52,280 --> 00:47:54,560
or I'm between jobs right now.

1108
00:47:54,560 --> 00:47:55,800
That sounds polite.

1109
00:47:55,800 --> 00:47:57,440
And what about students?

1110
00:47:57,440 --> 00:47:59,600
Students can say I'm a student.

1111
00:47:59,600 --> 00:48:03,600
I study business management or I'm still in university.

1112
00:48:03,600 --> 00:48:04,440
Perfect.

1113
00:48:04,440 --> 00:48:05,760
Now let's practice.

1114
00:48:05,760 --> 00:48:07,120
Emily, what do you do?

1115
00:48:07,120 --> 00:48:08,920
I'm a business English trainer.

1116
00:48:08,920 --> 00:48:12,360
I help professionals improve their communication skills.

1117
00:48:12,360 --> 00:48:13,480
That's a great answer.

1118
00:48:13,480 --> 00:48:14,440
My turn.

1119
00:48:14,440 --> 00:48:15,840
I'm a content creator.

1120
00:48:15,840 --> 00:48:18,760
I create educational podcasts and videos.

1121
00:48:18,760 --> 00:48:19,800
Very nice.

1122
00:48:19,800 --> 00:48:21,480
See how easy that is?

1123
00:48:21,480 --> 00:48:23,720
Yes, it's simple when you know the structure.

1124
00:48:23,720 --> 00:48:26,040
Now let's talk about where you work.

1125
00:48:26,040 --> 00:48:28,080
This is another common question.

1126
00:48:28,080 --> 00:48:30,760
Right, someone might ask, where do you work?

1127
00:48:30,760 --> 00:48:31,720
Exactly.

1128
00:48:31,720 --> 00:48:33,880
You can say, I work in an office

1129
00:48:33,880 --> 00:48:35,840
or I work in a hospital.

1130
00:48:35,840 --> 00:48:37,320
Or you can mention the company.

1131
00:48:37,320 --> 00:48:39,320
I work at a marketing agency.

1132
00:48:39,320 --> 00:48:41,160
Yes, and you can also say,

1133
00:48:41,160 --> 00:48:43,840
I work for a multinational company.

1134
00:48:43,840 --> 00:48:47,240
What's the difference between work at and work for?

1135
00:48:47,240 --> 00:48:48,320
Good question.

1136
00:48:48,320 --> 00:48:50,440
Work at is for a place.

1137
00:48:50,440 --> 00:48:53,600
Work for is for a company or employer.

1138
00:48:53,600 --> 00:48:54,680
That's clear.

1139
00:48:54,680 --> 00:48:55,640
Let me try.

1140
00:48:55,640 --> 00:48:59,320
I work at a bank and I work for a financial company.

1141
00:48:59,320 --> 00:49:00,160
Perfect.

1142
00:49:00,160 --> 00:49:01,000
You got it.

1143
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:02,560
What about remote work?

1144
00:49:02,560 --> 00:49:06,180
You can say, I work from home or I work remotely.

1145
00:49:06,180 --> 00:49:07,920
That's very common these days.

1146
00:49:07,920 --> 00:49:09,160
Yes, it is.

1147
00:49:09,160 --> 00:49:12,720
Now let's talk about describing your responsibilities.

1148
00:49:12,720 --> 00:49:15,800
This is where you explain what you actually do, right?

1149
00:49:15,800 --> 00:49:16,760
Exactly.

1150
00:49:16,760 --> 00:49:20,240
You can say, my main responsibility is to...

1151
00:49:20,240 --> 00:49:23,920
For example, my main responsibility is to manage a team.

1152
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:28,200
Yes, or my responsibilities include preparing reports,

1153
00:49:28,200 --> 00:49:31,480
attending meetings, and communicating with clients.

1154
00:49:31,480 --> 00:49:33,640
Let's give more practical examples.

1155
00:49:33,640 --> 00:49:36,200
Sure. I work in customer service.

1156
00:49:36,200 --> 00:49:40,040
I help customers solve problems and answer their questions.

1157
00:49:40,040 --> 00:49:41,320
I'm a project manager.

1158
00:49:41,320 --> 00:49:43,720
I plan projects, coordinate teams,

1159
00:49:43,720 --> 00:49:45,520
and ensure deadlines are met.

1160
00:49:45,520 --> 00:49:47,980
Excellent. And I'm an accountant.

1161
00:49:47,980 --> 00:49:51,320
I manage financial records and prepare budgets.

1162
00:49:51,320 --> 00:49:52,640
Very professional.

1163
00:49:52,640 --> 00:49:55,040
Notice how we use simple verbs.

1164
00:49:55,040 --> 00:50:00,040
Yes. Plan, manage, prepare, help, simple and clear.

1165
00:50:00,040 --> 00:50:04,240
Exactly. Now let's talk about describing a typical workday.

1166
00:50:04,240 --> 00:50:08,040
This is very useful in conversations and interviews.

1167
00:50:08,040 --> 00:50:11,640
You can say, I usually start my day by checking emails.

1168
00:50:11,640 --> 00:50:14,840
Then I attend meetings and work on my tasks.

1169
00:50:14,840 --> 00:50:18,840
In the afternoon, I focus on projects and communicate with clients.

1170
00:50:18,840 --> 00:50:21,840
I usually finish work around 6 p.m.

1171
00:50:21,840 --> 00:50:23,840
Let's give a full example.

1172
00:50:23,840 --> 00:50:28,840
Okay. I wake up at 7 a.m., get ready, and start work at 9.

1173
00:50:28,840 --> 00:50:32,840
I check emails, attend meetings, and work on reports.

1174
00:50:32,840 --> 00:50:35,520
After lunch, I focus on client communication.

1175
00:50:35,520 --> 00:50:37,880
I finish work at 6 p.m.

1176
00:50:37,880 --> 00:50:38,880
That's perfect.

1177
00:50:38,880 --> 00:50:40,280
Clear and structured.

1178
00:50:40,280 --> 00:50:42,280
Now let's talk about colleagues.

1179
00:50:42,280 --> 00:50:43,280
Yes.

1180
00:50:43,280 --> 00:50:46,480
You can say, I work with a team of five people.

1181
00:50:46,480 --> 00:50:49,280
Or you can say, I have supportive colleagues.

1182
00:50:49,280 --> 00:50:51,960
And you can say, I report to my manager.

1183
00:50:51,960 --> 00:50:55,200
If you are the manager, you can say, I lead a team.

1184
00:50:55,200 --> 00:50:56,200
Exactly.

1185
00:50:56,200 --> 00:50:59,000
Now let's talk about what you like about your job.

1186
00:50:59,000 --> 00:51:01,520
You can say, I enjoy working with people.

1187
00:51:01,520 --> 00:51:04,080
Or I like the flexibility of my job.

1188
00:51:04,080 --> 00:51:06,680
I love the creative aspect of my work.

1189
00:51:06,680 --> 00:51:08,840
I find my job rewarding.

1190
00:51:08,840 --> 00:51:10,480
These are great expressions.

1191
00:51:10,480 --> 00:51:12,800
Now what about challenges?

1192
00:51:12,800 --> 00:51:15,680
You can say, sometimes the workload is heavy.

1193
00:51:15,680 --> 00:51:18,800
Or it can be stressful during busy periods.

1194
00:51:18,800 --> 00:51:21,040
Meeting deadlines can be challenging.

1195
00:51:21,040 --> 00:51:23,120
Notice how we use polite language.

1196
00:51:23,120 --> 00:51:25,960
Yes, we don't say, I hate my job.

1197
00:51:25,960 --> 00:51:32,740
Exactly now let's do a role play great idea. Hi. Nice to meet you. What do you do? Nice to meet you, too

1198
00:51:32,740 --> 00:51:39,300
I'm a marketing specialist. I work for a digital marketing company. That sounds interesting. What do you do exactly?

1199
00:51:39,460 --> 00:51:46,800
My main responsibility is to create online campaigns and analyze their performance. That's great. Do you enjoy your job?

1200
00:51:46,960 --> 00:51:52,260
Yes, I do. I enjoy being creative and working with different clients. What about challenges?

1201
00:51:52,260 --> 00:51:55,760
Sometimes it can be stressful when deadlines are tight.

1202
00:51:55,760 --> 00:51:56,760
I understand.

1203
00:51:56,760 --> 00:51:58,280
That's very common.

1204
00:51:58,280 --> 00:51:59,280
What about you?

1205
00:51:59,280 --> 00:52:00,280
What do you do?

1206
00:52:00,280 --> 00:52:01,280
I'm a teacher.

1207
00:52:01,280 --> 00:52:03,260
I teach business English to professionals.

1208
00:52:03,260 --> 00:52:04,260
That sounds rewarding.

1209
00:52:04,260 --> 00:52:05,260
It is.

1210
00:52:05,260 --> 00:52:08,480
I enjoy helping people improve their communication skills.

1211
00:52:08,480 --> 00:52:09,480
Great conversation.

1212
00:52:09,480 --> 00:52:10,480
Yes.

1213
00:52:10,480 --> 00:52:11,480
Very natural.

1214
00:52:11,480 --> 00:52:14,160
Now, let's do a job interview example.

1215
00:52:14,160 --> 00:52:15,160
Good idea.

1216
00:52:15,160 --> 00:52:16,160
Good morning.

1217
00:52:16,160 --> 00:52:17,160
Can you tell me about yourself?

1218
00:52:17,160 --> 00:52:18,160
Good morning.

1219
00:52:18,160 --> 00:52:20,920
I am a sales manager with five years of experience.

1220
00:52:20,920 --> 00:52:26,520
I currently work at a retail company where I lead a team and manage sales strategies.

1221
00:52:26,520 --> 00:52:28,160
What are your main responsibilities?

1222
00:52:28,160 --> 00:52:33,640
I manage a team of 10 people, set sales targets, and analyze performance.

1223
00:52:33,640 --> 00:52:35,160
Why do you want this job?

1224
00:52:35,160 --> 00:52:39,920
I'm looking for new challenges and opportunities to grow professionally.

1225
00:52:39,920 --> 00:52:40,920
Excellent answer.

1226
00:52:40,920 --> 00:52:41,920
Thank you.

1227
00:52:41,920 --> 00:52:42,920
That was very useful.

1228
00:52:42,920 --> 00:52:45,720
Yes, it shows how to speak professionally.

1229
00:52:45,720 --> 00:52:47,440
Now let's quickly review.

1230
00:52:47,440 --> 00:52:49,880
We learned how to ask, what do you do?

1231
00:52:49,880 --> 00:52:52,060
And how to answer, I'm a.

1232
00:52:52,060 --> 00:52:54,580
We learned how to describe where you work.

1233
00:52:54,580 --> 00:52:56,840
And how to explain your responsibilities.

1234
00:52:56,840 --> 00:52:59,140
We practiced real conversations.

1235
00:52:59,140 --> 00:53:00,920
We learned useful phrases.

1236
00:53:00,920 --> 00:53:03,900
The most important thing is to keep it simple.

1237
00:53:03,900 --> 00:53:05,600
And speak with confidence.

1238
00:53:05,600 --> 00:53:07,240
Now it's your turn.

1239
00:53:07,240 --> 00:53:08,320
What do you do?

1240
00:53:08,320 --> 00:53:10,720
Write your answer and practice speaking.

1241
00:53:10,720 --> 00:53:12,420
Don't be afraid of mistakes.

1242
00:53:12,420 --> 00:53:14,480
Keep practicing every day.

1243
00:53:14,480 --> 00:53:16,660
Before we finish, thank you for listening.

1244
00:53:16,660 --> 00:53:19,080
Your support means everything to us.

1245
00:53:19,080 --> 00:53:24,800
learning and stay confident. See you next time. Goodbye everyone.
